Android's bionic libc never implemented the C11 pthread_barrier_* family:
it is missing from every API level the NDK ships, and there is no
libc symbol to link against. Mesa's u_thread.h gates its barrier on

    #if defined(HAVE_PTHREAD) && !defined(__APPLE__) && !defined(__HAIKU__)

which excludes Apple and Haiku but not Android, so an Android build takes
the pthread_barrier_t branch and fails:

    error: unknown type name 'pthread_barrier_t'; did you mean 'pthread_attr_t'?
    error: implicit declaration of function 'pthread_barrier_init'

The very next #else branch implements barriers with a mutex + condvar
through the vendored C11 threads shim (src/mesa/compat/c11/threads_posix.h,
which is a thin pthread wrapper), so it works on bionic unchanged.
Excluding Android from the first branch is therefore enough.

Only the barrier guard is touched: an identical guard a few lines above
(in util_thread_get_time_nano) selects pthread_getcpuclockid, which bionic
DOES provide, so it must keep taking the pthread branch.

diff --git a/src/mesa/util/u_thread.h b/src/mesa/util/u_thread.h
--- a/src/mesa/util/u_thread.h
+++ b/src/mesa/util/u_thread.h
@@ -282,7 +282,7 @@
  * util_barrier
  */
 
-#if defined(HAVE_PTHREAD) && !defined(__APPLE__) && !defined(__HAIKU__)
+#if defined(HAVE_PTHREAD) && !defined(__APPLE__) && !defined(__HAIKU__) && !defined(__ANDROID__)
 
 typedef pthread_barrier_t util_barrier;
 

--- a/src/virgl_util.c	2026-11-01 08:45:01.923557899 +0800
+++ b/src/virgl_util.c	2026-11-01 10:01:40.927556144 +0800
@@ -366,7 +366,13 @@
 
 void set_dmabuf_name(int fd, const char *name)
 {
-   #ifdef DMA_BUF_SET_NAME_B
+   /* Android's <linux/dma-buf.h> defines DMA_BUF_SET_NAME_B as
+    * _IOW(DMA_BUF_BASE, 1, u64), where u64 is a Linux kernel type that the
+    * NDK userspace headers never declare, so the ioctl below fails to compile:
+    *   error: use of undeclared identifier 'u64'
+    * The only callers are the amdgpu DRM renderers, which are compiled out on
+    * Android anyway (no libdrm), so the whole body is dropped there. */
+   #if defined(DMA_BUF_SET_NAME_B) && !defined(__ANDROID__)
    if (name && *name != '\0')
       ioctl(fd, DMA_BUF_SET_NAME_B, name);
    #else
